Let HarmonyOS's Password Vault fill and save passwords, behind a setting.

The vault answers apps that describe their login fields through
autoFillManager; reporting a field to the IME as a username or password only
changes the keyboard. With ohos.password_vault_enabled on (the shell's
"passwordVault" setting, off by default):

- Focusing a field of a parsed password form asks the vault once per form
  (chrome/browser/ui/ohos/password_vault_ohos.cc, through the engine HAR's
  "passwordvault" system service) and fills the account the user picks.
- Chromium's saved passwords are not sent to the renderer: no suggestions,
  no filling on load, no generation popup.
- A successful login goes to the vault, which asks whether to save, and is
  also saved into Chromium's store without a prompt, so turning the vault
  off later loses nothing.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-password-vault.patch

